1 to 2025, and February to March came in under 90% of normal in 36 of those 75 years on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 6 grids. In 2025 on that middle, July to August ran 66% of normal and November to December 63%. So far in 2026, March to April sat at 55% of normal on the middle. Grid 20282 shows August to September 2026 at a preliminary 75.5, an estimate from NOAA rain that can differ from RMA&rsquo;s final index.</p>"}
